# Line-ending policy: LF everywhere, except the bytes we redistribute verbatim.
#
# The default below is what makes this policy hold for files nobody thought to list.
# Everything Git detects as text is stored and checked out with LF regardless of platform,
# so a Windows checkout cannot reintroduce CRLF into a generated artifact, a provenance
# record or a script. Without it the rules were per-extension, and anything outside that
# list - provenance.json in particular - silently picked up CRLF on Windows and had to be
# normalised by hand before it could be committed.
#
# Verified safe when introduced: `git ls-files --eol` reported 317 tracked files already
# LF in the index and exactly 7 mixed, all of them the byte-exact ASAM schemas excluded
# below. So this pins the status quo rather than rewriting it.
#
# Order matters - later rules win, so every exception must stay below this line.
*          text=auto eol=lf

# The UML READMEs publish SHA-256 checksums of the committed *.scxml files. Without a rule
# here, a checkout with core.autocrlf=true rewrites them to CRLF, the published checksums
# stop matching, and re-committing normalises them back — churn that looks like a model
# change but is not one.
*.scxml    text eol=lf

# Generated RDF is written in canonical form by scripts/generate_semantic_artifacts.py and
# its checksums are recorded in provenance.json; same reasoning as above.
*.ttl      text eol=lf

# The ModelExport zip preserves the byte-exact Windows output of ShapeChange. It must never
# be touched by line-ending normalisation.
*.zip      binary

# Verbatim redistributions of ASAM deliverables are byte-exact by design and their
# checksums are published in the sibling README. Git must not convert them in either
# direction: the OpenDRIVE XSDs ship with CRLF, and normalising them would both break the
# documented checksums and misrepresent what was redistributed. This is the one place where
# CRLF in the index is correct, and verify-models.yml fails if it is ever "fixed".
standards/*/schema/**   -text
